<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">East Punjab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1947">1947</a>–<a href="/years/1950">1950</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> was the Indian province formed from the eastern part of British Punjab after the partition of 1947. Small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> and estates in the region were absorbed into it. In 1950 it became the state of Punjab, which was later divided to create <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a> and transfer hill areas to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/east-punjab.jpg" alt="East Punjab" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: EasiestMusiciono789 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_Punjab.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
